module Core

### Represents the protocol for implicit copy at assignment sites.
### `Assignable` gates the `=` operator and every position that implicitly copies a
### value: `var x = a`, passing as a non-`steal` argument, returning a non-`?T`
### value, and `with` lens-copy. Auto-derived for any type whose `@llvm` layout
### contains no `ptr` (and for `@llvm("void")`). Types with managed-pointer
### payloads (entities, `Retained[T]`, `Tracked[T]`, etc.) must opt in by writing
### `obeys Assignable` and a `$copy` body that spells out each field's verb,
### centralising the cost in one visible place.
protocol Assignable
  ### Returns a copy of this value suitable for binding into the destination slot.
  ### For auto-derived types this is a bitwise duplicate. For opt-in types the body
  ### performs whatever per-field work is required (refcount bump, deep clone,
  ### ownership transfer) so the cost is visible at one location instead of every
  ### call site.
  ### :returns: A copy of this value.
  @readonly
  routine Me.$copy() -> Me